# Non-relativistic classical mechanics: mathematical audit and expansion

2026-10-03. Research audit, not production acceptance or an engine receipt. Originals/imports remain read-only. The owner requires full prerequisite closure; the current explicitly formulated inventory now has complete conditional arguments, including E27–E30. This is local author review, not independent certification. The earlier broad OPEN inventory is replaced by actual arguments, explicit statements and a per-contract ledger; unresolved obligations are retained rather than hidden.

## Mathematical suppliers and actual proof uses

The baseline published-supplier-register.tsv preserves exact IDs, canonical paths, full Statement/Definition text, publication state, dependencies and pinned hashes. It previously recorded 47 direct interfaces and 1,458 inherited nodes. A registered inherited node is not automatically a missing prerequisite merely because its proof was not reread in this session; actual invalid or inadequate supplier uses matter. Hash checks are integrity checks, not proof certificates. Current relevant statement/proof/use inspections are recorded in expansion-supplier-review.json. Local M1–M10 are retained and E1–E26/D1 add explicit mathematical developments with purely mathematical dependencies.

Exact inspected uses in this expansion include:

| Canonical mathematical ID | Actual statement/proof use and hypotheses |
|---|---|
| `thm-picard-lindelof-local-existence-and-uniqueness`, `thm-banach-fixed-point` | Continuous time dependence/local state Lipschitz on an open cylinder; complete curve space and invariant short-time contraction. E2 also writes the contraction/completeness proof locally. M10 is compact continuation, never arbitrary global existence. |
| `thm-gronwall-integral-inequality` | Nonnegative continuous error inequality with explicit Lipschitz bound; E2 writes its exponential integrating-factor argument and E8/E15 derive the actual error inequalities before using it. |
| `thm-euclidean-inverse-function-theorem` | C¹ map, invertible derivative and genuine local inverse; M4/E7/E20 apply it only on nonsingular local branches, with no global inverse implied. |
| `thm-a-regular-level-set-is-an-embedded-submanifold`, `lem-linear-functional-annihilating-kernel-of-a-surjection-is-a-transpose-multiple` | Smooth nonempty full-rank regular fibre; finite-dimensional surjection and annihilating functional. M6/E20 supply the dynamic multiplier equation separately from extrema multipliers. E1 supplies SO(3) rank check. |
| `cor-real-spectral-theorem-for-self-adjoint-endomorphisms` | Finite real inner-product self-adjoint map; symmetry kills real-normal rotation blocks. M7 uses positive mass matrix square root and diagonalizes symmetric mass-scaled stiffness; M8 diagonalizes symmetric inertia, with semidefinite/degenerate cases retained. |
| `thm-jordan-canonical-form-from-pid-module-structure` | Finite complexification with split characteristic polynomial. Its module/companion-to-Jordan proof is adequate for E16's stable/unstable spectral decomposition; E16 supplies the exponential polynomial and nonlinear Lyapunov/cone argument itself. |
| `thm-poincare-recurrence-for-finite-measure-preserving-systems` | Measurable preserving map on finite measure space; no-return null towers then countable union of last-visit exceptions. E12 writes the actual proof and limits Hamiltonian applications to complete iterates on finite invariant regions. |
| `cor-c-one-change-of-variables-for-l-one-functions` | ACω, C¹ diffeomorphism of Euclidean open sets, integrable real/complex function and absolute Jacobian. The inspected proof goes compact-support substitution→rational boxes→Borel measure equality→completion→signed parts. E13 uses bounded smooth functions on bounded swept material regions, with positive J. |
| `thm-divergence-theorem-for-bounded-c-one-euclidean-domains` | ACω, n≥2, bounded C¹ domain and field C¹ up to closure; outward normal on each component. Its finite boundary-chart partition/local flux argument is adequate for E13's smooth material/control volumes and row-wise stress divergence. |
| `prop-commuting-hamiltonian-vector-fields-integrate-to-a-local-r-n-action`, `lem-stabilizer-of-the-r-n-action-on-a-compact-connected-regular-fibre-is-a-full-lattice`, `thm-compact-connected-regular-fibres-are-tori` | Independent involutive smooth integrals, compact connected regular fibre, ACω; tangent spanning implies open transitive orbits, compact quotient implies full discrete lattice. E18 explicitly verifies those model hypotheses before torus use. |
| `thm-liouville-arnold-action-angle-theorem` | ACω, all preceding fibre hypotheses plus saturated proper submersion with connected fibres over a ball. Its period-sheet/local-generation/closed-lattice/Lagrangian-section proof was inspected. An actual two-form prerequisite defect was found and is repaired locally by E21 before E18; no claim that the defective citation alone closes its proof. |
| `thm-cartans-magic-formula`, `thm-poincare-lemma-for-star-shaped-domains`, `cor-local-normal-form-for-submersions`, `cor-every-smooth-vector-field-on-a-compact-manifold-is-complete` | Smooth forms/fields; the published Poincaré statement covers ONE-forms only. Local submersion projection supplies a section; compact smooth vector fields are complete under ACω. Their actual relevant proofs were inspected. Closed two-form exactness needed in action-angle step 5.2 is supplied by E21, not the one-form statement. |

## Confirmed published supplier-use defect and local discharge

`thm-liouville-arnold-action-angle-theorem` Proof step 5.2 sets τ=σ*ω, a closed **two-form**, then cites `thm-poincare-lemma-for-star-shaped-domains` for τ=dα. That supplier states exactness of a closed C¹ vector field, equivalently a **one-form**. Its proof differentiates a scalar radial potential and does not establish the two-form claim. E21 gives the missing smooth radial one-form α and proves dα=τ by coefficient differentiation and the closure identity. Its earlier E1 handles the separate one-form lattice use. With these replacements the original action-angle conclusion and all valid hypotheses are preserved. Actual classical consumers are CM14 regular tori/action-angle and their local adiabatic use. Root owns canonical published-defect recording and any original repair; this directory supplies the replacement prerequisite only.

