## Scope integrity and remaining closure

All 151 canonical primary A contracts are represented in closure-ledger.json, including the SO(3) contract accidentally omitted by the old inventory parser. Mathematical sections have explicit purely mathematical deps and recomputed dependency levels. Fifteen proposed mathematical A/B homes retain budgets≤90/30; proof sections must be split into their distinct definition/lemma/result items before a production manifest, never counted as one item to evade the cap.

The defined checkpoint obligations are now discharged by complete arguments in mechanical-horseshoe.md(E27), analytic-kam.md(E28), analytic-backward-error.md(E29) and local-fluid-wellposedness.md(E30). Exact source reading and additional published/plan supplier interfaces are recorded in sources-advanced/reading-ledger.md and advanced-supplier-review.json. New arguments are local author-reviewed development, not independent acceptance.

Generic source-specific Melnikov claims, compressible/rough-wall/turbulence specialist theory and known-open global3D NS retain explicit future/conjectural scope. None is a hidden established premise; no valid specified theorem was removed. Framework-incompatible topics retain their destinations. Every current physical theorem consumes only the explicit mathematical branch and its stated adopted physical assumptions.
